 them to build new structured products."})},{question:"How are PreStocks backed?",answer:(0,n.jsx)(n.Fragment,{children:"PreStocks are fully backed by holding entities that are directly or indirectly invested in the underlying company."})},{question:"What does the price of PreStocks represent?",answer:(0,n.jsx)(n.Fragment,{children:"The price of PreStocks represents the gross price per share of the referenced company."})}],Mechanics:[{question:"What happens if the company goes public?",answer:(0,n.jsx)(n.Fragment,{children:"If the company goes public, the underlying positions are convertible (fully onchain, without KYC) into an equivalent tokenized public stock. Underlying shares may have a post-IPO lockup period (typically 6 months), during which liquidity may be limited and the PreStocks token price may trade at a discount to the public stock price. Holders will have up to 9 months after IPO (3 months after the 6 month lockup period) to convert their PreStocks tokens into the equivalent tokenized public stock. After the 9-month post-IPO conversion deadline, the tokens will expire worthless and will no longer be supported."})},{question:"What happens if the company gets acquired or merges with another company?",answer:(0,n.jsx)(n.Fragment,{children:"In a merger or acquisition, the underlying positions will resolve in one of two ways. If the deal is cash-based, net proceeds will be distributed pro rata as USDC, which holders can convert their PreStocks into. If the deal results in equity of the new company, PreStocks may become convertible into a tokenized version of that new company's equity, if we create and support one. Holders will have up to 6 months to convert after the conversion period opens. After that deadline, the tokens will expire worthless and will no longer be supported."})},{question:"What keeps PreStocks prices aligned with real-world prices?",answer:(0,n.jsx)(n.Fragment,{children:"Arbitrage. If PreStocks trade above real-world prices, arbitrageurs can buy exposure offchain and mint and sell PreStocks onchain for a profit, increasing supply and lowering the price. If PreStocks trade below real-world prices, arbitrageurs can buy onchain and sell the corresponding offchain exposure, reducing supply and raising the price. This helps keep PreStocks prices aligned with real-world prices."})}],Legal:[{question:"Are PreStocks available in all countries?",answer:(0,n.jsxs)(n.Fragment,{children:["No. PreStocks are unavailable in the United States, in any country subject to US, UK, or EU sanctions, or in any country where their use is prohibited by law. See the"," ",(0,n.jsx)(a(),{href:d.Cp,target:"_blank",className:"underline",onClick:()=>(0,c.lT)("terms-of-service","faq"),children:"Terms of Service"})," ","for the full list of Restricted Persons and Prohibited Jurisdictions."]})},{question:"Are PreStocks affiliated with the referenced companies?",answer:(0,n.jsx)(n.Fragment,{children:"No, PreStocks are not affiliated with, endorsed by, or issued by the referenced companies."})},{question:"What rights do I get as a PreStocks holder?",answer:(0,n.jsx)(n.Fragment,{children:"PreStocks provide indirect economic exposure to the underlying company through onchain liquidity with real-time price discovery. They do not confer any ownership, voting, dividend, information, or other legal rights."})},{question:"How can I verify that PreStocks are fully backed?",answer:(0,n.jsx)(n.Fragment,{children:"The issuer provides third-party attestation reports, published periodically or available on request if costs are covered, to confirm that all PreStocks are fully backed. You can compare the total supply in circulation to the figures in the report."})},{question:"Which entities provide the backing for PreStocks?",answer:(0,n.jsx)(n.Fragment,{children:"Each token product is backed by one or more vetted holding entities that verifiably own the underlying exposure. Counterparty legal names are not disclosed because they require contractual confidentiality to avoid unwanted solicitation, reputational targeting, and potential adverse actions from issuers or intermediaries. Preserving this confidentiality is often a precondition for participation; without it, institutions are materially less willing to tokenize positions, which would reduce available inventory and ultimately harm tokenholder liquidity."})}]};function u(){let e=(0,s.usePathname)(),t=(0,s.useSearchParams)(),[r,i]=(0,o.useState)(null),a=(0,o.useRef)([]),d=(0,o.useMemo)(()=>Object.keys(h).map(e=>({id:e,label:e})),[]),u=e=>{let t=e.get("tab");if(t){let e=d.find(e=>e.id.toLowerCase()===t.toLowerCase());return e?.id||"Overview"}return"Overview"},[p,m]=(0,o.useState)(()=>u(new URLSearchParams(t.toString())));(0,o.useEffect)(()=>{let e=u(new URLSearchParams(t.toString()));e!==p&&m(e)},[t]);let f=h[p]||h.Overview;return(0,o.useEffect)(()=>{if(null===r)return;let e=a.current[r];e&&e.scrollIntoView({behavior:"smooth",block:"start"})},[r]),(0,n.jsxs)("div",{className:"flex flex-col items-center w-full",children:[(0,n.jsx)("div",{className:"w-full bg-gradient-to-b from-primary/5 to-transparent pt-8 pb-6 md:pt-16",children:(0,n.jsx)("div",{className:"max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 md:px-6 lg:px-8",children:(0,n.jsxs)("div",{className:"text-center",children:[(0,n.jsx)("h1",{className:"text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl font-bold text-brand-front-primary mb-4",children:"Frequently Asked Questions"}),(0,n.jsx)("p",{className:"text-base text-brand-front-200 max-w-2xl mx-auto",children:"Common questions about PreStocks and how they work."})]})})}),(0,n.jsxs)("div",{className:"space-y-8 max-w-2xl mx-auto pb-[32rem] px-4 w-full",children:[(0,n.jsx)(l.A,{tabs:d,selectedTab:p,onTabChange:r=>{m(r),i(null);let n=new URLSearchParams(t.toString());"Overview"===r?n.delete("tab"):n.set("tab",r.toLowerCase());let a=n.toString(),s=a?`${e}?${a}`:e;window.history.replaceState(null,"",s)},showCount:!1}),(0,n.jsx)("div",{className:"space-y-4",children:f.map(({question:e,answer:t},s